<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/14th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Kalisz (1343)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1343">1343</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polish-teutonic-war-1326-1332">Polish–Teutonic War (1326–1332)</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of Kalisz, concluded in July 1343, ended a long conflict between King Casimir III of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teutonic-order">Teutonic Order</a>. Poland gave up its claims to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pomerelia">Pomerelia</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chelmno-land">Chełmno Land</a> and the Michałów Land, while the Order returned <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kuyavia">Kuyavia</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dobrzyn-land">Dobrzyń Land</a>, which it had occupied in the war of 1326–1332. The peace between the two powers lasted for over sixty years.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/treaty-of-kalisz-1343.jpg" alt="Treaty of Kalisz (1343)" width="320" height="304" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Poznaniak · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Polska_1333_-_1370.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
